    description: "## Origin\n\nFiled per the just-merged playbook §Phase U4 fourth bullet (process-validation-queue-with-bakeoffs-and-uat.md, PR #3580). hg-uat-v4.1.0 Round 06 verdict was 'moved' on the pre-committed quantitative criteria (12/12 ground-truth on chatwoot transitive controllers), AND Round 08 §8.4 falsified the claim-text mechanism (transitive base-class walk).\n\n## What the claim text describes vs. what the linker actually does\n\nWI-vigih's PR #194 description for the view_template sub-claim: 'Closes the cross-language framework-dispatch traversal gap in jackson_dispatch / kafka_streams_dispatch / view_template / react_component'. Helper extension: collect_transitive_base_names accepts meta_keys for kafka_streams's interfaces metadata key.\n\nThe view-template-linker-v1 actually resolves controller→template via Rails filename convention (`app/views/<controller-path>/<action>.<recognized-extension>`), NOT via a strict in-tree base-class walk.\n\n## Round 08 §8.4 falsification\n\n- **Forward direction**: 92 transitive-Rails controller actions in chatwoot reach ApplicationController via in-tree inheritance but have no view file at the conventional path. The linker emitted zero `renders` edges for any of them. A strict inheritance-walk linker would have emitted edges.\n- **Reverse direction**: 4 SuperAdmin::*Controller actions whose chain leaves the codebase mid-walk via the third-party Administrate gem still received correct `renders` edges (their view files exist at the conventional path). A strict in-tree inheritance-walk linker would have skipped them.\n- The two modalities yield observably DIFFERENT results, falsifying the inheritance-walk hypothesis. Path convention is the operative resolution.\n\n## Why needs_human_review (not todo_hard)\n\nPer the Phase U4 playbook fourth bullet: 'the choice between (a) update claim text vs (b) change linker behavior is a value judgment'. Both options are valid:\n\n(a) **Update the WI-vigih claim text** to describe the actual path-convention resolution. The linker's behavior is observably correct on chatwoot (12/12 transitive Rails actions resolved); the claim text just mischaracterizes the mechanism. Changes only documentation.\n\n(b) **Change the linker behavior** to actually validate the inheritance chain. This is a behavior change — would mean SuperAdmin::*Controller actions that reach into the third-party Administrate gem are no longer covered (currently they ARE covered because their view files exist at the conventional path). Trade-off: stricter mechanism guarantee vs. real-world coverage.\n\nThe asymmetry between linkers (django-orm-dispatch-linker-v1 walks inheritance and consequently misses HierarkeyForm chains per DQ-1; view-template-linker-v1 uses path convention and consequently DOES cover Administrate chains) is itself worth a design discussion.\n\n## What was already done in Phase U4\n\nWI-vigih's awaits_bakeoff_validation tag was stripped (campaign-wide WI-vigih strip — moved on jackson_dispatch R01 + kafka_streams R05 + view_template R06; the view_template moved-with-Mechanism-mismatch resolved per playbook fourth bullet). This item captures the orphaned reconciliation question.\n\n## References\n\n- Round 06 report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_artifacts/hg-uat-v4.1.0/lab-notebook/round-06-WI-vigih-view-template-transitive/report.md\n- Round 08 §8.4: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_artifacts/hg-uat-v4.1.0/lab-notebook/round-08-followup-discriminators/report.md\n- Master report §4 DQ-3: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_artifacts/hg-uat-v4.1.0/lab-notebook/master-report.md\n- Playbook §Phase U4 4th bullet: .agent/agent_playbooks_protocols_sops_skills/process-validation-queue-with-bakeoffs-and-uat.md\n- Producer: packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/view_template.py"  # 2075
